From: BDY-G98 port <noreply@example.invalid>
Date: Thu, 23 Jul 2026 16:35:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] usb: gadget: preserve RockUSB loader descriptor version

The RockUSB binding sets bcdUSB to 0x0201 so RKDevTool identifies it as
a Loader.  The composite GET_DESCRIPTOR path subsequently overwrites every
High-Speed gadget to 0x0200, making the same running U-Boot appear as
Maskrom.  Retain 0x0201 only for the RockUSB download function.

Signed-off-by: BDY-G98 port <noreply@example.invalid>
---
 drivers/usb/gadget/composite.c | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/usb/gadget/composite.c b/drivers/usb/gadget/composite.c
--- a/drivers/usb/gadget/composite.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/gadget/composite.c
@@ -1050,7 +1050,10 @@ static int composite_setup(struct usb_gadget *gadget,
 			if (gadget->speed >= USB_SPEED_SUPER) {
 				cdev->desc.bcdUSB = cpu_to_le16(0x0310);
 				cdev->desc.bMaxPacketSize0 = 9;
-			} else {
+			} else if (!strcmp(cdev->driver->name, "usb_dnl_rockusb")) {
+				/* Rockchip tools use bcdUSB bit 0 to identify Loader. */
+				cdev->desc.bcdUSB = cpu_to_le16(0x0201);
+			} else {
 				cdev->desc.bcdUSB = cpu_to_le16(0x0200);
 			}
 			value = min(w_length, (u16) sizeof cdev->desc);
-- 
